<title>USA: Southern Union Co Q3 shr $1.00 vs $1.16.</title>
<headline>Southern Union Co Q3 shr $1.00 vs $1.16.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>							    March 31,</p>
<p>							1997	    1996</p>
<p> Operating revenues		     $   313,931   $   275,028</p>
<p> Operating margin/a			    97,937	  96,574</p>
<p>Net earnings available for</p>
<p>  common stock				   17,678	  20,549</p>
<p>Net earnings per share/b:</p>
<p>   Primary					   1.00	    1.17</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				   1.00	    1.16</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>outstanding/b:</p>
<p>   Primary				   17,735,037    17,614,174</p>
<p>   Fully diluted			   17,761,419    17,654,189</p>
<p>							   Nine months ended</p>
<p>							    March 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	   1996</p>
<p> Operating revenues		     $   625,643   $   526,195</p>
<p> Operating margin/a			   215,289	 213,310</p>
<p>Net earnings available for</p>
<p>  common stock				   21,934	  23,697</p>
<p>Net earnings per share/b:</p>
<p>   Primary					   1.24	    1.36</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				   1.24	    1.35</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>outstanding/b:</p>
<p>   Primary				   17,725,398    17,461,870</p>
<p>   Fully diluted			   17,743,810    17,514,886</p>
<p>NOTE:  The Company's fiscal year-end is June 30.</p>
<p>Operating margin consists of operating revenues less purchased gas cost</p>
<p>All periods have been adjusted to reflect a five percent common stock dividend distributed on December 10, 1996.</p>
<p>The company said earnings were effected by an increase in bad debt accruals as a result of significant increases in delinquent customer accounts due to natural gas prices that more than doubled during the period.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
